<urn:atm:triage:finding/FTQ-025>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FTQ-025" ;
  triage:title "drain_shutdown_finalizer_threads_for_test() joins SHUTDOWN_FINALIZER_THREADS with no timeout — can hang entire test binary (tests.rs:591)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/tests.rs:591 — DaemonRequestDispatcher::drain_shutdown_finalizer_threads_for_test() joins all handles registered in the process-wide SHUTDOWN_FINALIZER_THREADS static without any deadline or timeout. If any finalizer thread is blocked on a mutex, socket, or I/O operation, the entire test binary stalls indefinitely. Cargo's default test runner has a process-level timeout but no per-test deadline, so a single blocked finalizer causes all subsequent tests in the binary to appear to time out. Additionally the #[serial] attribute serializes against other #[serial] tests but non-serial tests still run in parallel; if a parallel test holds a resource the finalizer thread needs, deadlock results with no bounded recovery. NOTE: This defect is pre-existing; it was not introduced by the FTQ-024 fix in S.4-FIX-R2, but was exposed in scope during round-limit QA-3 review of tests.rs. Fix: add a bounded timeout to drain_shutdown_finalizer_threads_for_test — join each handle with a deadline (e.g., channel or condvar with recv_timeout) and panic with a descriptive message if any handle does not complete within the bound (e.g., 5 seconds). Converts a potential silent hang into a deterministic test failure." ;
  triage:category "FTQ" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-S" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-05-09T20:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
